            <ArticleTitle>The effect of inhibitors of prostaglandin synthesis in primary dysmenorrhea studied with hysterometry.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-49</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The technique called hysterometry has been used for the quantitative evaluation of effect of naproxen sodium and naproxen on myometrial tension in vivo during dysmenorrhea. It was observed that &quot;uterine tonicity&quot; - the datum arrived at after hysterometric recording - decreased significantly during naproxen medication in comparison with placebo treatment. Decrease in uterine tonicity was well correlated with relief of pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
